commit message:
Basic test & test for sparse adjacency matrices

I am only checking for the most basic capabilities of the reader class;
there is not yet any proper error handling involved.

add support for skipping parametrized unit tests

Example:

    @parametrize
    class test(TestCase):

      @parametrize.skip_if(lambda nprocs: nprocs > 1 and not hasattr(os, 'fork'), 'nprocs>1 not supported on this platform')
      def check(self):
        ...

    test(nprocs=1)
    test(nprocs=2)

add {func,eval,expv2.ns}.{real,imag,conj}

This patch adds functions for taking the real or imaginary part or the
conjugate of a `function.Array` or `evaluable.Array`.

fix calling ctxt exits when Log.__enter__ fails

The following simplification of `Log` illustrates the issue:

    class Log(contextlib.ExitStack):
      def __enter__(self):
        self.enter_context(foo)
        ... # If an exception is raised here, `foo.__exit__` is not called.
        return super.__enter__()

This is fixed by adding an extra method, `Log._init_context(self, stack)`, that
is called in `Log.__enter__` to initialize the exit stack, wrapped in a `try
... except`:

    class Log():
      def __enter__(self):
        stack = contextlib.ExitStack()
        try:
          self._init_context(stack)
        except:
          stack.__exit__(*sys.exc_info())
        return self
      def _init_context(self, stack):
        ...

